expect: fail

# the standard library states every one of its levels rather than defaulting them, and this is the half of
# that which is observable: six names a program used to be able to write, refused at three different axes -
# `private` on a declaration is the file, nothing written is the module, and `private` on a member is the
# owner type. Two of them carry the sentence that used to be a comment asking nicely: mem.eco's byte
# allocator said "nothing outside this file should call these" and process.eco's `raw_argv` said it was
# public only because there were no modifiers yet
--- OUT --->
[error] InaccessibleDeclaration  stdlib_internals_are_not_reachable.eco:13:11

  'CH_DOT' is internal to the module 'stdlib', so the module 'main' cannot name it. Write 'public' on the declaration to make it part of what 'stdlib' offers.

  12 | 
  13 | echo str::CH_DOT;
     :           ^^^^^^
  14 | 

  150 | internal const uint8 CH_SPACE = 32;
  151 | internal const uint8 CH_DOT = 46;
      :                      ------ declared here
  152 | internal const uint8 CH_ZERO = 48;

